      "week": 8,
      "title": "Governance and Politics",
      "description": "This week focuses on the role of the government in shaping the trajectory of AI. We begin by examining the current state of frontier AI regulation, which mainly exists in the form of state laws. We then turn to a study of the macro-strategies that governments could take in the face of advanced AI. Next, we study two important governance tools: compute governance, and liability, and weigh the costs and benefits of each. Next, we learn about the various dimensions of the US-China AI race, and consider what policies could help the US stay ahead. Finally, we take stock of what the Democratic majorities in the newest congress mean for AI.",
